course: dictionary
lesson: 12100
title: Living together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Coexist is made of two parts: co- means together, and exist means to be or live. So to coexist means to live or be together at the same time and in the same place. «Rabbits, foxes and owls coexist in the same wood.» All three live there at the same time.
explain: You can also coexist peacefully. This means living together and getting along, even when you are different. «People of many religions and cultures coexist peacefully in our city.» Being different does not stop them being good neighbours.
explain: Coexist is often used with the word with. «Deer coexist with farmers on the hills.» Here the deer and the farmers share the same land. When you meet coexist, ask yourself: are two or more things living together at the same time?
fact: Coexist is a verb, and coexistence is the noun for the idea: «coexistence» means living together.
fact: «Coexist» means to live or exist together at the same time and in the same place.
fact: «Coexist peacefully» means to live together in harmony, even though you are different.
fact: In science, different animals coexist in a habitat, such as a pond, where frogs, fish and insects all live together.
fact: The verb changes its form: coexist, coexists, coexisted, coexisting.
exercise: «Bees and birds coexist in the garden.» What does coexist mean here? | To travel far away from each other | *To live together in the same place at the same time | To hide from one another | To fight until only one side is left
exercise: Which word is the noun for the idea of living together? | coexists | coexisted | *coexistence | coexist
exercise: «Many families coexist peacefully on our street.» Which word tells you the families get on well? | families | street | many | *peacefully
test: Which phrase means living together in harmony even though people are different? | Sleep in | Travel far | Shout loudly | *Coexist peacefully
test: Fill the gap: «Yesterday, two villages ___ in the valley.» | *coexisted | coexistence | coexist | coexisting
exam: Which sentence uses coexist correctly? | «Foxes coexisted rabbits.» | «Foxes and rabbits coexist yesterday loudly.» | *«Foxes and rabbits coexist in the same wood.»
